  <div class="chart-container">
    {charts['performance']}
  </div>

  <h3>GPA Progression: A Concerning Pattern</h3>
  <p>The longitudinal view across three exam periods reveals a critical trend: students improve sharply from Previous GPA to SSC (+0.262 points on average), but then <strong>regress significantly from SSC to HSC (-0.244 points)</strong>. The net change from Previous GPA to HSC is a marginal +0.018—essentially flat. This "progression collapse" suggests that whatever factors drive SSC success are not sustained through the HSC cycle.</p>

  <div class="insight-box danger">
    <strong>System Effectiveness Alert</strong>
    The HSC-to-SSC regression of −0.244 GPA points is the single most important finding in this dataset. It implies that the education system is failing to maintain student trajectories during the final secondary years. Interventions should target the SSC-to-HSC transition specifically, not just foundational learning.
