  <p>This section examines the relationship between family income, parent education, internet access, and private tuition on HSC outcomes. <strong>Effect sizes are universally small</strong> (Cohen's d < 0.05), indicating that in this sample, socio-economic advantage does not translate into measurable academic advantage at the HSC level.</p>

