  <p>Students whose parents have Secondary education achieve the highest mean HSC result (4.050), while those with Graduate-educated parents score lowest (4.001). The difference between the highest and lowest parent-education groups is 0.086 GPA points. ANOVA confirms no significant difference across parent education levels (F = 1.020, p = 0.383).</p>

