  <h3>Public vs. Private: Context-Dependent</h3>
  <p>The public-private performance gap varies dramatically by district. In Dhaka, public schools outperform private schools by 0.234 GPA points (4.179 vs. 3.945). In Rajshahi, the reverse holds: private schools lead by 0.173 points (4.169 vs. 3.996). This heterogeneity implies that <strong>institutional type is less important than local implementation</strong>. A "one size fits all" policy favoring either public or private expansion would be misguided.</p>

